        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Minoan civilisation</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, with settlements and strong influence on Thera, Kythera, Melos, Kea and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> and at Miletus on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> today)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 3100–1100 BCE; the first palaces from c. 1900 BCE, the height of the new palaces c. 1700–1450 BCE, then Mycenaean Greek rule from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knossos">Knossos</a> and a long decline</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The palaces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knossos">Knossos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phaistos">Phaistos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-malia">Malia</a> and Zakros; wall paintings and scenes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bull-leaping">bull-leaping</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamares-ware">Kamares ware</a>, carved sealstones and goldwork; the undeciphered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linear-a">Linear A</a> script; trade across the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">Excavated palaces, towns, tombs and sanctuaries (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-evans">Arthur Evans</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knossos">Knossos</a> from 1900, the Italian mission at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phaistos">Phaistos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikolaos-platon">Nikolaos Platon</a> at Zakros, Spyridon Marinatos at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akrotiri-prehistoric-city">Akrotiri</a> on Thera); seals and inscriptions in scripts that cannot be read; Egyptian and Mesopotamian records; later Greek myth and writers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a></span></div>
        </div>
