    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>From about 1900 BCE the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>’s first palaces, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knossos">Knossos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phaistos">Phaistos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-malia">Malia</a>: complexes of courts, storerooms and workshops that organised the island’s wealth.</li><li>Their wall paintings, carved seals, fine pottery and images of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bull-leaping">bull-leaping</a> influenced the whole <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, and their ships carried their trade to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>.</li><li>Their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linear-a">Linear A</a> script is still undeciphered; after about 1450 BCE Mycenaean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knossos">Knossos</a>, and the name “Minoan” itself is modern, taken from the mythical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minos">King Minos</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Wall paintings in Minoan style have been found far from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, at Tel Kabri in present-day Israel and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Tell el-Dab’a</a>, the ancient Avaris in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a>, where they include scenes of young athletes leaping over bulls.</p></aside>
    </section>

